#### 4. Mystery Guest (Smell 2)
**Test:** `ImportOrders_FromCsv_ParsesCorrectly` (line 140)
```csharp
File.ReadAllText(@"C:\TestData\orders.csv")
```
**Problem:** Depends on a file at a hard-coded Windows path. Will fail on any machine where that file doesn't exist (CI, Linux, teammate's laptop).
**Fix:** Use an inline string or embedded resource:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ImportOrders_FromCsv_ParsesCorrectly()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    const string csvData = "SKU-1,2\nSKU-2,1\nSKU-3,3\nSKU-4,1\nSKU-5,2";

    var orders = processor.ImportOrders(csvData);

    Assert.AreEqual(5, orders.Count);
}
```
**Risk:** Test only passes on one developer's machine; guaranteed CI failure.

> **Note:** This finding also qualifies as **Resource Optimism** (extended smell) — the test assumes `C:\TestData\orders.csv` exists without any guard.

