### 🟡 MEDIUM

#### 5. Eager Test (Smell 5)
**Test:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (line 52)
```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
Assert.AreEqual("Completed", order.Status);
```
**Problem:** Calls **7 distinct production methods**. A failure in any one makes diagnosis ambiguous — is it validation, discounting, payment, or inventory?
**Fix:** Test each method independently; if you need an integration-level workflow test, mark it explicitly:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Integration")]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { ... }
```
**Risk:** Slow diagnosis; one broken method masks failures in all others.

