## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Why First |
|----------|-------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | 5 min | Test is verifying **nothing** — immediate false confidence |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | 10 min | One branch is silently untested every run |
| 3 | Mystery Guest | 5 min | Test is **broken** on every machine except one |
| 4 | Sleepy Test | 10 min | Flaky + 2 s wasted per run |
| 5 | Exception Handling | 5 min | One-line swap to `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` |
| 6 | Magic Number + Assertion Roulette | 10 min | Fix together — same test method |
| 7 | Sensitive Equality | 10 min | Assert on structured properties |
| 8 | Eager Test | 15 min | Split or tag as `[TestCategory("Integration")]` |
| 9 | General Fixture | 2 min | Delete unused `_logger` field |

**References:** Peruma et al., *tsDetect* (ESEC/FSE 2020); Spadini et al., *Severity Thresholds* (MSR 2020); Camara et al., *Flaky Test Prediction* (SAST 2021). Full catalog: [testsmells.org](https://testsmells.org/).
